e><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Joint</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Carr</surname><given-names>NG</given-names></name><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Isolation and molecular characterization of five marine cyanophages propagated on <italic>Synechococcus </italic>sp strain WH7803</article-title><source>Applied and Environmental Microbiology</source><year>1993</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>3736</fpage><lpage>3743</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16349088</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waterbury</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Valois</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Franks</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Platt T, Li WKW</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Biological and ecological characterisation of the marine unicellular cyanobacterium <italic>Synechococcus</italic></article-title><source>Photosynthetic picoplankton</source><year>1986</year><volume>214</volume><publisher-name>Canadian Bulletin of Fisheries and Aquatic Sciences</publisher-name><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>120</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hennes</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Suttle</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fluorescently Labeled Virus Probes Show That Natural Virus Populations Can Control the Structure of Marine Microbial Communities</article-title><source>Applied and Environmental Microbiology</source><year>1995</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>3623</fpage><lpage>3627</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16535146</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fuhrman</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Marine viruses and their biogeochemical and ecological effects</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1999</year><volume>399</volume><fpage>541</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10376593</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/21119</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hewson</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Govil</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Capone</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Carpenter</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuhrman</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence of <italic>Trichodesmium </italic>viral lysis and potential significance for biogeochemical cycling in the oligotrophic ocean</article-title><source>Aquatic Microbial Ecology</source><year>2004</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>8</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilhelm</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Suttle</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Viruses and Nutrient Cycles in the Sea &#x02013; Viruses play critical roles in the structure and function of aquatic food webs</article-title><source>Bioscience</source><year>1999</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>781</fpage><lpage>788</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/1313569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuller</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Joint</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Charpy L, Larkum AWD</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of cyanophage diversity and population structure in a south-north transect of the Atlantic Ocean</article-title><source>Marine Cyanobacteria</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>Monaco: Bulletin de l'Institut Oceanographique</publisher-name><fpage>209</fpage><lpage>216</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuller</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Joint</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Mann</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Bell CR, Brylinsky M, Johnson-Green P</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of cyanophage diversity in the marine environment using denaturing gradient gel electrophoresis</article-title><source>Microbial Biosystems: New Frontiers Proceedings of the 8th International Symposium on Microbial Ecology Atlantic Canada Society for Microbial Ecology</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Halifax, Canada</publisher-name><fpage>565</fpage><lpage>570</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDaniel</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Houchin</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Williamson</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Paul</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Plankton blooms &#x02013; Lysogeny in marine <ita